Written $X <: Y$, a formal ordering on types meaning "$X$ is a ${fref("/01-programming-language-theory/02-concepts/subtype.td")} of $Y$" - $X$ substitutes for $Y$.

Written $X <: Y$, a formal ordering on types meaning "$X$ is a ${fref("/01-programming-language-theory/02-concepts/subtype.td")} of $Y$" - $X$ **substitutes for** $Y$.
